noindex: true
version: 0.2.0
author: Temper Tools
desc:Temper Control Hub
// Temper Control hub. One instance per FX chain. Each destination parameter's
// native Parameter Modulation link points at one of the slot `out` sliders
// below; the hub computes macros, LFOs, envelope followers and the 12 slot
// outputs once per audio block. Its entire state is its sliders (saved,
// undone, duplicated and automated natively); the Lua side never runs in the
// audio path. Audio passes through unchanged (the followers only listen).
//
// The slider layout is the CTRL1 schema and is APPEND-ONLY once shipped.
// scripts/lua/lib/temper_control_layout.lua generates the slider block below
// (scripts/lua/tools/gen_control_sliders.lua) and
// tests/lua/test_control_jsfx_layout.lua enforces byte parity, the base
// offsets below and div_tab against the layout and the engine.
//
// Engine twin (scripts/lua/lib/temper_control_engine.lua, transcribed
// literally; tests/probes/control/probe_parity.lua compares the two live):
// curves (crv), connection and slot maths, the hash (hash01), slew / smoothing
// (smooth_step), the LFO shapes (lfo_shape) and the sync divisions (div_tab).
// JSFX-only, no Lua twin: the envelope-follower detector (@sample), the LFO
// phase sources (play_position / beat_position while playing, free-running
// seconds while stopped), solo masking, and the first-block seeding of the
// smoothing / held state from the saved sliders.
//
// Header slider 3 (`seed`, "global seed") is RESERVED: CTRL1 never reads it
// (each LFO has its own lfo.n.seed). It exists so the slot stays append-only.
//
// Unreferenced LFO/follower units are skipped and their out sliders are left
// as they are.
//
// Restart rule (0.2.0): restarts happen only while playing. A playing block
// jumped on a stopped-to-playing edge (transport start, render start), a
// backwards move (seek back, loop wrap) or a forward move of more than
// max(0.5 s, 16 blocks) (seek ahead; playrate up to 4x stays under it). On a
// jumped block the LFO and slot smoothing snap to their targets and the
// followers restart from silence. The LFO phase reads the timeline only while
// playing; stopped, it runs on the free counters, so a cursor click while
// stopped never pops the preview. The first block after load is not a jump: it
// keeps the seeding from the saved sliders. s_held (an inactive absolute A
// holding its last contribution) is routing state and is kept.

in_pin:in 1
in_pin:in 2
in_pin:in 3
in_pin:in 4
in_pin:in 5
in_pin:in 6
in_pin:in 7
in_pin:in 8
out_pin:out 1
out_pin:out 2
out_pin:out 3
out_pin:out 4
out_pin:out 5
out_pin:out 6
out_pin:out 7
out_pin:out 8

